{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791029526,"nonce":"1tounFDMVeAG+Vlc+aspHrX4gOE=","title":"SVG \u003ctext\u003e never draws: the font database is empty","message":"resvg is built with `text`, `system-fonts` and `memmap-fonts`, and the\nCargo.toml comment claimed SVG text rendering therefore worked. It did\nnot. Those features only let usvg convert text to paths; it still needs\na populated font database to shape with, and all three parse sites used\n`usvg::Options::default()`, whose `fontdb` is empty. Every `\u003ctext\u003e`\nelement resolved to no glyphs and vanished.\n\n    \u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\u003e\u003ctext x=\"0\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"28\"\n      fill=\"currentColor\"\u003eM\u003c/text\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\n\ndrew zero pixels. A circle in the same place drew fine, which isolates\nit to the database rather than the rasterizer.\n\nSites: `rasterize::RasterizedSvg::from_data`, `document::from_data` and\n`document::extract_element_metadata`.\n\nFixed by a process-wide `OnceLock\u003cArc\u003cusvg::fontdb::Database\u003e\u003e` that\nloads system fonts on first use, attached by a shared\n`rasterize::options_for`. Scanning system fonts is slow and most SVGs\nBlinc draws are path-only icons, so the scan is gated on the source\nactually containing a `\u003ctext\u003e` ELEMENT — matched so that an id, class or\ncomment containing \"text\" does not drag the fonts in.\n\nReported by the ashui session, which hit it once it started sending full\nSVG markup through usvg.\n\nNot done: SVG text uses system fonts, not the faces blinc_text has\nregistered. Pointing both at one database would let SVG text match the\nUI's fonts.","files":null}]}